IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `td78-nouns`

-- Row il-78. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: the instruments, the regulations, the items of the 2007 amending regulations, the laws and the order that the two items read, item I1 and item I2, and the dates the pages print.
-- Tests of the controls and of the readings are in td78-tests-controls.l4, and the two assertions that FAIL on purpose (one per item) are in td78-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:regs:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation of the preference regulations (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py,
-- and N is the line number in the whole page, which the header of the excerpt lists.
-- The excerpt of the Law's consolidation is deposited and is read by tools/srcquote.py and tools/hebcheck.py, but no line of it is quoted in this module.
-- `ext:[xxNNN-pPPP]` lines quote the Hebrew printed on the deposited image of Kovetz HaTakanot (kt) or Sefer HaChukim (sh) issue NNN, printed page PPP (registers/source-bundle/pages/).
-- Every Hebrew string typed below is a stretch of the ext: line above it (or of a src: line), and tools/hebcheck.py checks that each Hebrew run of this module is in an excerpt or on an ext: line.
-- Where a quotation mark is printed around a term, the ext: line types the Hebrew gershayim, and the consolidation prints a different pair of marks.
-- Superscript footnote marks printed in the words are not typed.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.
-- The Kovetz HaTakanot files come from an archive of the printed issues that is not an official site; the Sefer HaChukim files come from the Knesset's site, which is official.

§ `References`

-- ===== THE INSTRUMENTS. An issue date is the date the footer of the issue prints; it is NOT a commencement date. =====

